'''Thomas Alvin Morga'''  is an American stuntman, stunt coordinator, and actor best known for his various roles in ''[[Star Trek]]'' and for being the only actor to play [[Jason Voorhees]], [[Leatherface]] and [[Michael Myers (Halloween)|Michael Myers]].<ref>{{Cite web|date=August 10, 2020|title=The Only Actor To Play Michael Myers, Leatherface & Jason Voorhees|url=https://screenrant.com/tom-morga-actor-michael-myers-jason-voorhees-leatherface/amp/|access-date=June 1, 2021|website=ScreenRant|language=en-US}}</ref>

== Career ==
Morga began stunt work in the mid-1970s. He later began working as a stunt double for [[Patrick Duffy]] in ''[[Man from Atlantis]]''. Since then, Morga has doubled for several actors in feature films and television. His work also includes stunt and non-stunt acting roles in numerous ''[[Star Trek]]'' films and television episodes. However he only received credit for a very little number of his appearances.

== Jason Voorhees, Leatherface and Michael Myers ==
In 1985, Morga portrayed [[Jason Voorhees]] in ''[[Friday the 13th: A New Beginning]]'' during Tommy's hallucinations except for the opening dream sequence where he was played by stuntman John Hock who was personally selected by him to fill-in during his absence. He also stunt-doubled for Dick Wieand, who played Jason's imposter Roy Burns during the film playing him in almost all masked scenes except for a few filmed with Hock.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.fridaythe13thfranchise.com/2011/06/rtccl-chat-with-john-hock-jasonroy-part.html|title=A Chat with John Hock (Jason Voorhees/Roy Burns, Friday the 13th Part 5)}}</ref> He portrayed [[Leatherface]] in the bridge scene of ''[[The Texas Chainsaw Massacre 2]]''. He also portrayed [[Michael Myers (Halloween)|Michael Myers]] in the first half of ''[[Halloween 4: The Return of Michael Myers]]'', but was ultimately replaced by [[George P. Wilbur]].{{Citation needed|date=March 2022}} In 2009, he appeared in a documentary film ''[[His Name Was Jason: 30 Years of Friday the 13th]]''.<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.blu-ray.com/His-Name-Was-Jason-30-Years-of-Friday-the-13th/274790/ |title=His Name Was Jason: 30 Years of Friday the 13th (2009) |access-date=2024-07-08 |via=www.blu-ray.com}}</ref> In 2013, he was interviewed in a documentary film ''[[Crystal Lake Memories: The Complete History of Friday the 13th]]''.

== Awards ==
Morga was co-winner of a 2007 [[Taurus World Stunt Awards|Taurus World Stunt Award]] for "Best Fight" in ''[[Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Man's Chest]]''. He was also part of the stunt team nominated for a 2007 [[Screen Actors Guild Award]] nomination for "Outstanding Performance by a Stunt Ensemble in a Motion Picture" in ''[[Pirates of the Caribbean: At World's End]]''.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0604426/awards |title=Awards for Tom Morga |publisher=Internet Movie Database |accessdate=November 9, 2008}}</ref>

