'''Alex Diehl''' (born 26 November 1987 in [[Traunstein]]) is a German singer and songwriter.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.deutsche-mugge.de/interviews/4562-alex-diehl.html|title=Alex Diehl - Deutsche Mugge|publisher=|accessdate=25 February 2016}}</ref> He was selected as one of ten artists to compete in the [[Germany in the Eurovision Song Contest 2016|German qualifiers]] for the [[Eurovision Song Contest 2016]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Germany to send one of these 10 musicians to Eurovision |publisher=[[Deutsche Welle]] |url=http://www.dw.com/en/germany-to-send-one-of-these-10-musicians-to-eurovision/a-18973960 |date=12 January 2016 |accessdate=25 February 2016}}</ref> German televoters selected his entry ''{{lang|de|Nur ein Lied}}'' ("Just a Song") into the final of three, where he finished second only to [[Jamie-Lee Kriewitz]]' winning title ''[[Ghost (Jamie-Lee Kriewitz song)|Ghost]]''.<ref>{{cite news |title=Jamie-Lee Kriewitz to represent Germany |work=eurovision.tv |publisher=[[European Broadcasting Union|EBU]] |url=http://www.eurovision.tv/page/news?id=jamie-lee_kriewitz_to_represent_germany |date=25 February 2016 |accessdate=25 February 2016}}</ref>

